er":"Operates in computer hardware; annual sales are CNY 164.8 billion.","evidence":[{"quote":"FY2025: revenue 164781997658.23; grossProfit 8046993422.96; margin = grossProfit / revenue.","url":"https://eodhd.com/financial-apis/stock-etfs-fundamental-data-feeds/","filed":"2026-10-01T09:05:44.166Z","section":"Calculated from annual statements"},{"quote":"000977.SHE: Inspur Electronic Information Industry Co., Ltd., together with its subsidiaries, provides cloud computing and big data services in China and internationally. The company offers computing equipment, including storage, intelligent network, and cloud operating systems; software products, such as intelligent ERPs, enterprise and industry PaaS platforms, and databases; government and enterprise cloud services; and industrial internet products comprising industrial internet platform, safety, communication, equipment, application, supply chain, and equipment health management. It also provides comprehensive data management; mobile private and all-optical networks, 5G router, IoT gateways, and edge desktop cloud; intelligent terminals, which include display, zero-carbon, and service terminals, as well as intelligent robots; and software and information technology outsourcing and data center services. In addition, the company is involved in the development, production, and sale of computer hardware, software, and auxiliary equipment, as well as parts and electronic components; import and export; software technology development; and repair services. It serves manufacturing, metallurgy, chemical, telecommunications, food, building, water affairs, smart city, business, energy, healthcare, park, highway, urban rail, civil aviation, port and shipping, agriculture, water conservancy, education, culture and tourism, and supply chain industries. The company was formerly known as Langchao Electronic Information Industry Co., Ltd. and changed its name to Inspur Electronic Information Industry Co., Ltd. in April 2006. Inspur Electronic Information Industry Co., Ltd. was founded in 1998 and is headquartered in Jinan, China.","url":"https://eodhd.com/financial-apis/stock-etfs-fundamental-data-feeds/","filed":"2026-09-29","section":"Company description"}],"basis":"computed","chart":{"label":"Gross margin","unit":"percent","points":[[2016,0.13026648940390761],[2017,0.09980689541461485],[2018,0.10105698027396971],[2019,0.10993840743473901],[2020,0.10988207088746266],[2021,0.10447031240276078],[2022,0.10611152719990354],[2023,0.0935846220628822],[2024,0.06403143260384285],[2025,0.04883417810997811]]}},{"question":2,"answer":"Margins ranged from 4.9% to 9.4% during 2023–25; it earns 12.9% on its capital.","evidence":[{"quote":"FY2023: grossProfit / revenue = 9.4%.","url":"https://eodhd.com/financial-apis/stock-etfs-fundamental-data-feeds/","filed":"2026-10-03T18:25:33.456Z","section":"Calculated from annual statements"},{"quote":"FY2024: grossProfit / revenue = 6.4%.","url":"https://eodhd.com/financial-apis/stock-etfs-fundamental-data-feeds/","filed":"2026-10-03T18:25:33.456Z","section":"Calculated from annual statements"},{"quote":"FY2025: grossProfit / revenue = 4.9%.","url":"https://eodhd.com/financial-apis/stock-etfs-fundamental-data-feeds/","filed":"2026-10-03T18:25:33.456Z","section":"Calculated from annual statements"},{"quote":"10-year return on capital observations [[2016,0.048120586509530286],[2017,0.08387709230889946],[2018,0.2853901183046182],[2019,0.19742350109066284],[2020,0.3937535767720499],[2021,0.1489228609731868],[2022,0.11778729312460234],[2023,0.11157833691732573],[2024,0.11546967866930631],[2025,0.14012051914897808]]; median 0.1289539061367902. ROIC follows the displayed moat series; financial companies use return on tangible equity.","url":"https://eodhd.com/financial-apis/stock-etfs-fundamental-data-feeds/","filed":"2026-10-03T18:25:33.456Z","section":"Calculated from annual statements"}],"basis":"computed","chart":{"label":"return on capital","unit":"percent","points